=== parse\_condition
<sdocs-src.seiche.affected_population.parse_condition>
#block[
```py
parse_condition(expr: str) -> Callable[..., object]
```

]
Return a condition callable from a boolean expression string.

The condition has signature `(h, v, t) -> bool mask`. The expression is
evaluated with `eval` against an empty `__builtins__` namespace, so no
builtins or arbitrary names are reachable; only `h`, `v`, `t`, `True`
and `False`.

Parameters:

- #strong[`expr`]
  (#link("https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#str")[`str`])
  -- Boolean expression on `h`, `v` and `t`, e.g. `"h > 0.3"`.

Returns:

- #link("https://docs.python.org/3/library/collections.abc.html#collections.abc.Callable")[`Callable`]
  -- Function of signature `(h, v, t)` returning a boolean mask matching
  the input type.

Raises:

- #link("https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#NameError")[`NameError`]
  --

  If the expression references any name other than `h`, `v`, `t`, `True`
  or `False`.

Examples:

See the `param.pop.conditions` documentation.

