Estimate water depth using a simple method based on DEM and flood extent
mask.

Parameters:

- #strong[`dem`] (`ndarray`) -- Digital Elevation Model (DEM) as a 2D
  numpy array.
- #strong[`wet_mask`] (`ndarray`) -- Boolean or binary mask array where
  flooded pixels are True/1.
- #strong[`method`] (`SimpleMethod`) -- Method to use for estimation: -
  \'all\': Use the global maximum water surface elevation. - \'each\':
  Use the maximum per connected group of flooded pixels.

Returns:

- `ndarray` -- Estimated water depth per pixel (same shape as dem).

