=== compute\_gpkg\_sha256
<sdocs-src.seiche.utils_qol.compute_gpkg_sha256>
#block[
```py
compute_gpkg_sha256(
    filepath: str, layer: str | None = None
) -> str
```

]
Return a reproducible SHA-256 hash for a GeoPackage.

GeoPackage files contain internal timestamps / UUIDs that change on
every write, which would break a naïve file\_digest approach. The
function therefore reads the vector data (optionally a specific layer),
converts it to CSV text and hashes that deterministic representation.

Parameters:

- #strong[`filepath`]
  (#link("https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#str")[`str`])
  -- Path to the .gpkg file.
- #strong[`layer`]
  (#link("https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#str")[`str`]` | None`,
  default: `None` ) -- Name of the layer to hash. If None the default
  layer is used.

Returns:

- #link("https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#str")[`str`]
  -- Hexadecimal SHA-256 digest of the CSV representation of the
  geopackage contents.

